  "id": "delayed-reinforcement",
  "term": "delayed reinforcement",
  "definition": "Delayed reinforcement is reinforcement in which an action’s outcome or reward comes after a time gap rather than immediately. This delay can make learning the action–outcome relationship harder for reinforcement learning systems.",
